#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186091951 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092382 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "db808f48-6d0c-5b35-9342-b1817df65172" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Equation of a Tangent Line to a Curve at a Point"}] :question/id #uuid "2f5afc63-6988-5676-b170-5826e659a5fd" :question/math-academy-id "e-144" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y = 2x^3 - 2x$ at the point $(1,0).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x) = 2x^3 - 2x.$ Computing the derivative $f'(x)$ gives\n\n$$\nf'(x)  = 6x^2-2.\n$$\n\nWe then compute $f'(1)$, which gives\n\n$$\nf'(1)  = 6(1)^2-2 = 4.\n$$\n\nFinally, we use the point-slope form with $m=4$ and the coordinates of our point $(1,0),$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-0 & =4(x-1) \\\\ y & =4x-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186091952 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092383 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "84c8ba29-95c9-5494-be0b-9b67bee6e45c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining where a Tangent Line Intersects an Axis"}] :question/id #uuid "e248bb90-ba83-5e3f-938b-2c8be7d6eb7a" :question/math-academy-id "e-146" :question/problem "Find where the tangent to the curve $y=4\\sqrt{x}+4x$ at the point $(1,8)$ intersects the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=4\\sqrt{x}+4x.$ Let's first calculate the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4\\sqrt{x}+4x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{x}^{1/2}+4x) \\\\  & =2{x}^{-1/2}+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the slope of the tangent at our point is\n\n$$\nm=f'(1) = 2(1)^{-1/2}+4 = 6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the tangent is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-8 & =6(x-1) \\\\ y & =6x-6+8 \\\\ y & =6x+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find where the tangent line intercepts the $x$-axis, we set $y=0$ and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =6x+2 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point of intersection is $\\left(-\\dfrac 1 3, 0\\right).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092505 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092383 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "84c8ba29-95c9-5494-be0b-9b67bee6e45c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining where a Tangent Line Intersects an Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34ceb6d1-9f92-5a12-a620-1703269e2fea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(10,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241642} {:answer/id #uuid "757fd2b2-e67b-5b73-9960-69177e752366" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242224} {:answer/id #uuid "a8be58b9-3641-56b3-b019-b90b2aeec263" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,-10)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242661} {:answer/id #uuid "b3fb07a2-de66-5a8e-85f1-f9637a4db061" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-7,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242752} {:answer/id #uuid "d09a2270-6b9d-566d-955f-7ca56a000f84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,10)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243019}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d09a2270-6b9d-566d-955f-7ca56a000f84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,10)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243019} :answer-field/id #uuid "894232d0-aa75-55b0-8b57-14b37f42a79f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243697}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b75358e5-0e2f-554f-8ca2-4e81d5f869f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-10831" :question/problem "Find where the tangent to the curve  $y=\\frac{5}{x}-2x$ at the point $(1,3)$ intersects the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=\\frac{5}{x}-2x.$ Let's first calculate the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{5}{x}-2x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5{x}^{-1}-2x) \\\\  & =-5{x}^{-2}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the slope of the tangent at our point is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={f}^{′}(1)=-5(1)^{-2}-2=-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the tangent is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(3) & =-7(x-1) \\\\ y & =-7x+7+3 \\\\ y & =-7x+10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find where the tangent line intercepts the $x$-axis, we set $x=0$ and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-7(0)+10 \\\\ y & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point of intersection is $(0,10).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524004 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092382 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "db808f48-6d0c-5b35-9342-b1817df65172" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Equation of a Tangent Line to a Curve at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54e4cc66-ca5e-5066-be7f-ca8af81230be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3x-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523426} {:answer/id #uuid "8cb0ab78-979b-5380-82ce-790749223f04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523544} {:answer/id #uuid "ace4e43a-b577-57d5-86e7-009ce005e861" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-3x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523617} {:answer/id #uuid "b03cce63-0693-5a60-aa91-ea45127e8ffe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-3x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523623} {:answer/id #uuid "c490d8c0-eb7b-5865-8a42-1e154ab559fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2x-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523666}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8cb0ab78-979b-5380-82ce-790749223f04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523544} :answer-field/id #uuid "48f4ddec-7d82-5ded-b4ef-c0b8b5d933e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523825}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b262293b-c158-5061-ba4d-49a88b31e09c" :question/math-academy-id "q-10838" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y={x}^{2}+5x$ at the point $(-1,-4).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)={x}^{2}+5x.$ Computing the derivative ${f}^{′}(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+5x)=2x+5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute ${f}^{′}(-1)$, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(-1)=2(-1)+5=3\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we use the point-slope form with $m=3$ and the coordinates of our point $(-1,-4),$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-4) & =3(x-(-1)) \\\\ y+4 & =3(x+1) \\\\ y & =3x+3-4 \\\\ y & =3x-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244130 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092382 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "db808f48-6d0c-5b35-9342-b1817df65172" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Equation of a Tangent Line to a Curve at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "748ad103-47d7-54bd-b443-632c57c8e9a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242215} {:answer/id #uuid "799ee3bc-dfca-510e-a47e-2798dc153aad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=9x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242252} {:answer/id #uuid "89381a2f-8eb7-5360-9a54-f2019ea37a2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242387} {:answer/id #uuid "9a5d73c8-4cd6-5c27-8738-bda84fae71b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-9x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242528} {:answer/id #uuid "cf2facc4-edc5-55d0-8918-89250d81d554" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243007}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89381a2f-8eb7-5360-9a54-f2019ea37a2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242387} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6c47791-5d33-5c21-ab34-809782a452e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243762}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "59f7c071-253d-534f-b5b0-303aefe3edb7" :question/math-academy-id "q-10841" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y={x}^{2}-6x$ at the point $(3,-9).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)={x}^{2}-6x.$ Computing the derivative ${f}^{′}(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}-6x)=2x-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute ${f}^{′}(3)$, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(3)=2(3)-6=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we use the point-slope form with $m=0$ and the coordinates of our point $(3,-9),$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-9) & =0(x-3) \\\\ y & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523939 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092382 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "db808f48-6d0c-5b35-9342-b1817df65172" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Equation of a Tangent Line to a Curve at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6ebadb2-b0d8-5d8c-881b-669e826c4db0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523739}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6ebadb2-b0d8-5d8c-881b-669e826c4db0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523739} :answer-field/id #uuid "db7afdf7-4a01-5e98-a4e2-00e845a3f731" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523900}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "25f1b261-6dfa-5b14-a68c-dd89758e1b4c" :question/math-academy-id "q-342351" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y=\\frac{1}{16}{x}^{4}$ at the point  $(2,1).$\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=\\frac{1}{16}{x}^{4}.$ Computing the derivative ${f}^{′}(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{16}{x}^{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}\\cdot 4{x}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute ${f}^{′}(2)$, which gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(2)=\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot {2}^{3}=2.\n$$\n\nFinally, we use the point-slope form with $m=2$ and the coordinates of our point $(2,1),$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-1 & =2(x-2) \\\\ y & =2x-4+1 \\\\ y & =2x-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523927 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092382 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "db808f48-6d0c-5b35-9342-b1817df65172" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Equation of a Tangent Line to a Curve at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d6a12bc-5df9-5ffb-a1d6-d59cc5be5827" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x}{2}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523347}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d6a12bc-5df9-5ffb-a1d6-d59cc5be5827" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x}{2}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523347} :answer-field/id #uuid "81cb03e6-1a48-5ebf-a4ee-b237e415735b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523854}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "08550377-8abe-5e0e-9fca-2cd79ce06f39" :question/math-academy-id "q-342365" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y=-2\\sqrt{x}$ at the point $(4,-4).$\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=-2\\sqrt{x}.$ Computing the derivative ${f}^{′}(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2\\sqrt{x}) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x}) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{1/2}) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute ${f}^{′}(4)$, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(4) & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we use the point-slope form with $m=-\\frac{1}{2}$ and the coordinates of our point $(4,-4),$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-4) & =-\\frac{1}{2}(x-4) \\\\ y+4 & =-\\frac{1}{2}x+2 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{2}x+2-4 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{2}x-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523985 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092383 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "84c8ba29-95c9-5494-be0b-9b67bee6e45c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining where a Tangent Line Intersects an Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43d0b8c0-c0d0-53db-bf82-544dfd04bbd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523393}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43d0b8c0-c0d0-53db-bf82-544dfd04bbd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523393} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f19ea6a-73e1-5c5e-b2a8-31f8cd789cfa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523830} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f860ae67-ca2e-5e42-9e11-aa9ed6864a39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523774}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f860ae67-ca2e-5e42-9e11-aa9ed6864a39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523774} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1dfc637-f59d-5645-b5ba-dba9a1d16ea2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523912}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8bcad8aa-5196-5826-97b4-5ca478a3c38f" :question/math-academy-id "q-342378" :question/problem "Find where the tangent to the curve $y={x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}$ at the point  $(-1,-2)$ intersects the $y$-axis.\n\nThe tangent intersects the $y$-axis at\n$($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}} $).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)={x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.$ Let's first calculate the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3}-{x}^{-2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{-2}) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}-(-2{x}^{-3}) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}+\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the slope of the tangent at our point is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={f}^{′}(-1) \\\\  & =3(-1)^{2}+\\frac{2}{(-1)^{3}} \\\\  & =3-2 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the tangent is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-2) & =1\\cdot [x-(-1)] \\\\ y+2 & =x+1 \\\\ y & =x+1-2 \\\\ y & =x-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find where the tangent line intercepts the $y$-axis, we set $x=0$ and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =0-1 \\\\ y & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point of intersection is $(0,-1).$"}]}
